```cpp
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

__device__ __forceinline__ float sum19(float value)
{
    const unsigned int rank =
        threadIdx.x + blockDim.x *
        (threadIdx.y + blockDim.y * threadIdx.z);
    const unsigned int lane = rank % 32u;
    constexpr unsigned int mask = 0x0007ffffu;

    float sum = value;
    for (int offset = 16; offset >= 1; offset >>= 1) {
        const unsigned int partner = lane + offset;
        const bool has_partner = partner < 19u;
        const int source = has_partner
            ? static_cast<int>(partner)
            : static_cast<int>(lane);

        const float other = __shfl_sync(mask, sum, source, 32);
        if (has_partner) {
            sum = sum + other;
        }
    }
    return __shfl_sync(mask, sum, 0, 32);
}
```

Usage contract: exactly physical lanes 0–18 of the same warp call `sum19` once for this collective operation, each supplying its float. Lanes 19–31 must not call it. No full-warp ballot or implicit lockstep is required.

**Addition order and proof:** Write the original inputs as `a[i]`. Initially lane `i` holds only `a[i]`. Process offsets 16, 8, 4, 2, 1 in that order, always adding the partner’s pre-stage sum to the caller’s pre-stage sum. After the stage with offset `d`, lane `i` contains exactly the inputs at indices `i + k*d < 19`, with the nesting determined by these successive additions. Before that stage, its own sum contains the even multiples of `d`, while the partner’s sum contains the odd multiples. These sets are disjoint and together give the claimed set; if the partner is absent, the odd set is empty. Thus after offset 1, lane 0 contains every input exactly once. The sixth shuffle broadcasts that result to every caller.

**Collective validity:** Every caller’s bit is in `mask`, and all 19 named lanes execute each corresponding shuffle with the same mask and width. Every source is either a partner below 19, the caller itself, or lane 0, so every source participates in that same collective. Partnerless lanes still execute the shuffle. The `_sync` collectives provide the required rendezvous despite independent thread scheduling; this reasoning does not rely on implicit lockstep. Floating-point rounding follows the stated tree order; finite inputs can still overflow during addition.

Use a fold, a 16-lane butterfly all-reduction, and a three-source redistribution. Every caller executes six float shuffles; the last shuffle does not broadcast one lane’s completed sum.

```cpp
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

__device__ __forceinline__ float sum19(float value)
{
    const unsigned int rank =
        threadIdx.x + blockDim.x *
        (threadIdx.y + blockDim.y * threadIdx.z);
    const unsigned int lane = rank % 32u;
    constexpr unsigned int mask = 0x0007ffffu;

    // Fold inputs 16, 17, 18 into lanes 0, 1, 2.
    const int fold_source = static_cast<int>(
        lane < 3u ? lane + 16u : lane);
    const float extra = __shfl_sync(mask, value, fold_source, 32);
    float sum = value;
    if (lane < 3u) {
        sum = __fadd_rn(sum, extra);
    }

    // All-reduce the 16 folded values.
    for (unsigned int distance = 1u; distance <= 8u;
         distance <<= 1u) {
        const int source = static_cast<int>(
            lane < 16u ? (lane ^ distance) : lane);
        const float other = __shfl_sync(mask, sum, source, 32);
        if (lane < 16u) {
            sum = __fadd_rn(sum, other);
        }
    }

    // Three distinct sources deliver results to the extra lanes.
    const int result_source = static_cast<int>(
        lane >= 16u ? lane - 16u : lane);
    return __shfl_sync(mask, sum, result_source, 32);
}
```

